# HC-044 reference notes

SYNTHETIC_TRAINING_ONLY

This is a short exercise summary of public GitHub documentation and release notes, not a product schema or live repository observation.

## Boundaries to preserve

- A positive code-review assessment, a formal Approve review event, permission to approve, and permission to count that approval toward a requirement are separate.
- Whether one event is eligible is separate from whether enough distinct eligible approvals exist.
- A path rule applies to the changed-file set as a whole; one matching file does not establish that all changed files are covered.
- A review on an old head and a duplicate event cannot be counted as new evidence for the current head.
- Repository settings alone may be insufficient when effective organization or enterprise policy is unknown.
- Approval evidence alone does not establish that CI, conversations, deployments, or other merge gates pass.

